  "result_text": "H2 STATUS: UNRESOLVED\n\nGOVERNING SKILL TEXT: \"Derive hypothesis status from the latest effective outcome of each test entry (the original outcome unless a dated amendment supersedes it); never edit status directly. The status set is closed: `REFUTED` when the hypothesis's declared necessary prediction failed under an adequate test, `UNRESOLVED` otherwise.\" Also: \"An established deviation makes the reconciled outcome `NON_DISCRIMINATING` when the procedure that record evidences did not adequately test the preregistered prediction, unless evidence from outside the return verifies the deviation harmless.\"\n\nREASONING: H2's only test, T2, is reconciled as NON_DISCRIMINATING. The worker compared 2026-06-09 with 2026-06-11 instead of the preregistered 06-10 vs 06-11, so the necessary prediction (flat p95 between 06-10 and 06-11) was never tested. REFUTED needs that prediction to fail under an adequate test, and no adequate test exists. The worker's own CONTRADICTED label and its +1.6% figure belong to the wrong date pair, so they cannot refute H2.\n\nThe Data-validity note (census data, 0.1ms resolution) shows that a correct 06-10 vs 06-11 reading would have discriminated. It does not make the 06-09 reading a test of the prediction. H2 is also a causal claim with no identifying design, which would independently keep an exposure-outcome contrast from refuting it.\n\nA 06-10 vs 06-11 query would be the one test that could change this. The budget is spent and further metered queries are not authorized, so the skill's stop rule gives \"stop with limits\". H2 stays an open possibility, and the missing piece is the 06-10 `gateway_lat` reading, which needs authorization.\n\nI wrote this to `work/answer.md` in the working-files directory. I wrote no ledger file, so I ran no validator."
